# A client on the LAN listener gets exactly what the robot itself uses, in the direction the robot
# uses it, and nothing else. The robot connects with its serial as its client id, so these are its
# topics and nobody else's.
#
# The command topic is read-only here. The server commands the robot over the internal listener,
# which has no ACL, so no LAN client can ever hold write access to it, and a command left behind
# as a retained message cannot happen either.
pattern read prod/LR4/%c/command
pattern write prod/LR4/%c/state
pattern write prod/LR4/%c/activity
